WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:04.690
"It is a truth universally acknowledged,
that a single man in possession of a

2
00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.540
good fortune must be in want of a wife."

3
00:00:08.590 --> 00:00:11.410
A carriage rolls up to a grand house.

4
00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:14.510
A rich stranger has arrived
in the neighbourhood.

5
00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:19.520
At a smaller house down the road, five
sisters and their mother turn to look.

6
00:00:19.570 --> 00:00:20.470
Truth.

7
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:22.560
Universally acknowledged.

8
00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:24.510
It sounds so certain.

9
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:26.540
But should you believe it?

10
00:00:26.590 --> 00:00:31.040
In this mission, you'll trace how the plot
moves across the novel's three volumes,

11
00:00:31.090 --> 00:00:33.650
and what Austen first called it.

12
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:38.740
You'll learn four kinds of irony, where
words don't simply mean what they say.

13
00:00:38.790 --> 00:00:41.450
And you'll read the
opening chapter closely,

14
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:43.490
one sentence at a time.

15
00:00:43.540 --> 00:00:47.590
Your mission: decide whether you
should believe that first line.
